# Full-stack TypeScript

- Strict TypeScript. Public contracts are interfaces. No `any`.
- Routes validate input, call a service, and map `AppError` to JSON. No domain logic in routes.
- Integrations live in `/services`. Read environment only through `/config/env.ts`.
- HTTP shapes shared by client and server live in `/config/contracts.ts`.
- One module, one job. Extend a placeholder method instead of adding a second client.
- Prefer `fetch` over a new dependency.
- Placeholder methods stay generic until a feature is specified.

```ts
const message = readSendSms(req.body);
const result = await thrivewave.sendSMS(message.to, message.text);
res.status(202).json(result);
```
